82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (EcoChef addresses a common household problem: food waste caused by the inability to identify practical recipes from available ingredients with no existing tool that works offline or supports multilingual input.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [63]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (The project's core objective is to develop a cross-platform AI kitchen assistant capable of detecting ingredients via camera or text input, suggesting matching recipes in real time, and operating fully offline. Four goals guided the development: \(G1\) accurate single-frame ingredient detection using a mobile-deployable YOLO model, \(G2\) recipe suggestions delivered within 2 seconds online and under 5 seconds offline, \(G3\) full Turkish-language support via a built-in ingredient dictionary and LRU-cached translation, and \(G4\) a production-ready, containerised system with secure authentication and persistent user data.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [64]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 18 0 R
/E (The system employs YOLOv8 for real-time visual detection, Llama GGUF for on-device NLP inference, and the Spoonacular & TheMealDB APIs for access to 365,000+ recipes, backed by a FastAPI backend and React Native mobile client. Three research questions shaped the design: whether a single YOLOv8 model can reliably detect ingredients under varied conditions \(RQ1\), how effectively a quantised local LLM can substitute cloud-based NLP in resource-constrained environments \(RQ2\), and the impact of a multilingual ingredient dictionary on retrieval accuracy for nonEnglish users \(RQ3\).)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [65]
>>
endobj
